W: 1. Bring me a sheep, dear Mother, I'm tired of my brother.
W: If you need wool have the hind quarters shaved.
W: Don't bring a feeble old ewe; rams give you horns to hold to,
W: England is bad enough, but Scotland's depraved.
W:
W: 2. Bring me a llama, mama, dressed up in plaid pyjamas,
W: With garters of leather, sure that's what I crave.
W: 'tis said from Skye to Greenock, Scots have a way with livestock,
W: England is bad enough, but Scotland's depraved.
W:
W: 3. Bring out the sheets of rubber, grease them with peanut butter,
W: Or if you prefer, you can use mayonnaise.
W: Put on your mask of leather, whip me with sprigs of heather.
W: England is bad enough, but Scotland's depraved.
%
